      "body": "## Summary\n- Code follow-up to docs PR #45318 for issue #45317.\n- CUDA graph replay never runs PyTorch forward hooks, so configured `forward_hooks` can silently never fire.\n- Log a startup warning when `forward_hooks` are set and CUDA graphs are enabled, and point users at `--disable-decode-cuda-graph` / `--disable-prefill-cuda-graph` (or the matching Engine kwargs) if they need hooks on every forward pass.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `PYTHONPATH=python:test python3 test/registered/unit/model_executor/test_hook_manager.py`\n- [ ] Confirm the warning appears at server startup when `forward_hooks` are configured and CUDA graphs are enabled\n- [ ] Confirm no warning when CUDA graphs are disabled or no hooks are configured\n\nFixes #45317\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40349464509](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40349464509)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40349477161](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40349477161)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40349463918](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40349463918)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
